{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546969-why-no-dark-ages-game","id":1546969,"title":"Why no Dark Ages game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-14T10:17:22-08:00","id":1546969,"title":"Why no Dark Ages game?","content":"I'm a huge fan of the setting and I've been storytelling for more than 2 decades (continuosly so, I need to add, as unfortunately most ST I know only ST for events, with &quot;one shot&quot; stories, etc, while my chronicles usually span many years, often with the players starting as mortals) and I've been into Dark Ages since it was published. While we had &quot;Vampire Redemptiom&quot; (which was a masterpiece, even if flawed), since then we haven't got A SINGLE game set in the Dark Ages. <br /> <br /> While I still play many modern stting games, more recently the graphic novels, &quot;Coteries of New York&quot; and &quot;Shadows of New York&quot; (I unfortunately didn't like the thrd game in the trilogy and asked for a refund), I naturally miss playing my favourite setting that is the Dark Ages. I'm currently playing &quot;Parliament of Knives&quot; and I'm loving it, but I can't understand why not a single game set in another time. I often ask myself if the Dark Ages line wasn't that successful commercially, because I struggle to understand &quot;why on the Tellurian&quot; is that.<br /> <br /> I have read many of the Dark Ages romances and every book published and we could have many interesting stories to explore there, not to mention develop new ones. I really wished we had a game in the Dark Ages line. Havve you ever wondered why is that as well? Or am I the only &quot;Dark Ages lover&quot; here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T12:51:03-08:00","id":1546976,"title":"","content":"I do have some fondness for the Dark Ages line, but I wonder if it has to do with the Star Wars prequals as it's not easy to get invested in the story as we know what is going to happen to such and such a person. Though to be fair we all take creative liberties with the metaplot setting and change things around such as maybe Gesu of the Tzismce clan didn't suffer from final death at the end of the 4th Crusade and went into topor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T13:01:29-08:00","id":1546982,"title":"","content":"Why no Dark Ages (video) game? Because Paradox has already admitted that they massively overextended themselves in the late 2010s and branched out into a lot of IPs that are outside their core niche (many of which have not been successful). As such the current executive team is paring down on everything that isn't the traditional strength of in-depth strategy games. When they haven't even gotten Bloodlines 2 out, the idea that we're going to see any other big games from anywhere else in the larger WoD back catalogue is distant chance at best unless something major changes.<br /> <br /> If we see Dark Ages out of Paradox, it'll be something like an official version of the Crusader Kings mod to reskin CK as Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T13:05:45-08:00","id":1546984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546969-why-no-dark-ages-game?p=1546976#post1546976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have some fondness for the Dark Ages line, but I wonder if it has to do with the Star Wars prequals as it's not easy to get invested in the story as we know what is going to happen to such and such a person. Though to be fair we all take creative liberties with the metaplot setting and change things around such as maybe Gesu of the Tzismce clan didn't suffer from final death at the end of the 4th Crusade and went into topor.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good point, inded. In fact, that's why I encourage changes as much as I can, at least to this &quot;small background details&quot; like the one you mention about Gesu (I hate the idea to basically &quot;discard&quot; such an intersting character) or even something more drastic as I do sometimes that is to make it so that Saulot was actually diablerized or make it clear that the Giovanni failed to destroy the Capadocians. But perhaps you're right, that people don't get as much invested because they feel they &quot;know how the story is going to unfold&quot; and TC made such A TERRRIBLE MISTAKE of railroading the game and giving the impression that players can't do shit, that it possibly traumatized players around the world who thought it would be cool to change the seetting. In any case, I've been STing basically EXCLUSIVELY Dark Ages and Mage the Sorcerer's Crusade/Dark Ages Mage for 2 decades and I always make one change or another, the world feels very different each time and it's awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 12-14-2024, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T13:08:35-08:00","id":1546986,"title":"","content":"The Tzismce faction in Constaniople by Night was the best faction imho and that's all I have to say about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T13:56:14-08:00","id":1546995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546969-why-no-dark-ages-game?p=1546986#post1546986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tzismce faction in Constaniople by Night was the best faction imho and that's all I have to say about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! They really made a good job of making the clan interesting, much better imho than the &quot;freakshow&quot; that was so popular when the Tzimisce came to the fold(and unfortunatelly continued to be since...). I loved the whole thing about Dracon, Gesu and Symeon and its ties to Michael and the Dream, I remember at the time I first read the book I was just so curious about The Dracon and still the setting ended up never giving us his character sheet, but nowadays I prefer it that way, as they tend to many times ruin a character when making a bad character sheet, even though they made a somewhat good job with Michael, The Patriarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-24T19:34:49-08:00","id":1547231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546969-why-no-dark-ages-game?p=1546982#post1546982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why no Dark Ages (video) game? Because Paradox has already admitted that they massively overextended themselves in the late 2010s and branched out into a lot of IPs that are outside their core niche (many of which have not been successful). As such the current executive team is paring down on everything that isn't the traditional strength of in-depth strategy games. When they haven't even gotten Bloodlines 2 out, the idea that we're going to see any other big games from anywhere else in the larger WoD back catalogue is distant chance at best unless something major changes.<br /> <br /> If we see Dark Ages out of Paradox, it'll be something like an official version of the Crusader Kings mod to reskin CK as Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A8MO7fkZc5o\" target=\"_blank\">Sad but true</a> indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546969-why-no-dark-ages-game?p=1546995#post1546995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes! They really made a good job of making the clan interesting, much better imho than the &quot;freakshow&quot; that was so popular when the Tzimisce came to the fold(and unfortunatelly continued to be since...). I loved the whole thing about Dracon, Gesu and Symeon and its ties to Michael and the Dream, I remember at the time I first read the book I was just so curious about The Dracon and still the setting ended up never giving us his character sheet, but nowadays I prefer it that way, as they tend to many times ruin a character when making a bad character sheet, even though they made a somewhat good job with Michael, The Patriarch.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the book has some issues in my old grumpy opinion even i feel they are minor and Constantinople by Night is a pretty decent book overall. In fact their social division-spiritual narrative for the clans in the Dream helped me with fleshing out and fill dots for a bunch of stuff related to the rest of the Tzimisce, specially the &quot;Strahd expies&quot; aristocratic lord of night types, ironically.<br /> <br /> (Random aside, i've used Michael The Patriarch stats straight out of the book - except for extra dots in Auspex, Fortitude &amp; Mortis - for Cappadocius while STing the Giovanni Chronicles. Saulot too can work, but honestly the narrative of Michael's descent in religious mania/messiah complex just fits old 'Cappie to a degree i'm amazed to have never bumped into any discussion of the subject)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-24-2024, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-25T00:28:57-08:00","id":1547232,"title":"","content":"Because Vampire the Masquerade: Redemption already exists? :&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-25T10:31:39-08:00","id":1547241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546969-why-no-dark-ages-game?p=1547232#post1547232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Vampire the Masquerade: Redemption already exists? :&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>That Bloodlines already exists did not stop the development of Bloodlines 2 or the recent spate of Masquerade-related videogames, why should Redemption be impediment for anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-04-2025, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-25T12:03:56-08:00","id":1547242,"title":"","content":"An open-world game like Witcher 3 set in the WOD would be cool, but it looks like it will never happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28340-boldkill","name":"Boldkill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28340_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-25T14:02:06-08:00","id":1547244,"title":"","content":"Even if Paradox was in a position (financially and in terms of in-house technical expertise) to make a DA WoD game in the vein of the Witcher series... the problem is what's the market for Witcher, but you play as a vampire? We here, are obvious fans of the concept, but a AAA release is a huge investment by the company, and results have been really hit or miss in the industry. A single player game like The Witcher 3 had to sell ~35 million copies to break even (it sold ~50 million, so big success), because there's a lot less additional monetization available in single player games compared to game types that support more microtransactions/etc. <br /> <br /> Even with a bunch of visual novels and interactive fiction games, and some actual RPGs now, we can see that there is an audience for VtM video games... but is there a &quot;will sell 35 million copies&quot; market? Probably not. So what's the hook to bring in the millions of broad audience? If you weren't a WoD fan, and you were looking a The Witcher 4 (or whatever From Software does to one-up Elden Ring for a different style of dark Medieval-ish fantasy action RPG), or a new Dark Ages WoD game from a company that's never delivered this kind of game before... what's going to push you into taking that leap?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-25T14:06:28-08:00","id":1547245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boldkill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546969-why-no-dark-ages-game?p=1547242#post1547242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An open-world game like Witcher 3 set in the WOD would be cool, but it looks like it will never happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the part that they would need to get right for the game is the &quot;verticality&quot; of play rather than the open world aspect. Every vampire game might have different storylines, but they all fit into the same mold of you are a low-level character who gets caught up in everyone else's issues and bumbles one's way through them to change the status quo. But you don't change your relative power level or societal ranking.<br /> <br /> To use Skyrim as an example, you can become Thane of every hold, but never the Jarl. You can be guild master of the Companions, Mage College, Thieves Guild, and the Dark Brotherhood at the same time but never King/Queen of Skyrim. You might be Dragonborn but never the new Emperor.<br /> <br /> A good VtM game that wants to stand out has to take into account that if your character is successful enough, they will become the leader/power player simply by virtue of killing everyone who messes with you and no one else is strong enough to take the job. Bloodlines 1 allows you to choose your faction, but despite being strong enough to wipe out most of the power players, you are still just a cainite doing fetch quests. You don't become the new Prince/Baron/etc. and even if you did, the game ends without that being a mechanic to play with.<br /> <br /> But if you try to include that aspect of verticality to the game play, then you are practically forced to switch game genres to accommodate it. Rather than playing an RPG for the whole game, about halfway through it would suddenly shift into a City Builder/RTS/Management game system on top of your personal role play sections. Despite the climb for power being a central concept of the setting, I find that most people don't resonate with achieving those goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-25T18:48:23-08:00","id":1547247,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms, that is a good question. Ultimately, every RPG gamer wants it all, but I am reminded of why I fell in love with the WOD setting when thinking about your question. Politics! Navigating Kindred society, finding out Clan or sect secrets, surviving powerplays by manipulating elders, and carving out a niche for oneself. That has to be the difference otherwise it would become like any other vampire game, kill monsters and eat people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28340-boldkill","name":"Boldkill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28340_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-25T19:05:34-08:00","id":1547248,"title":"","content":"Thoth, I agree with you. We need a game where choices matter, but we also need a game where there are so many different paths that it makes replaying the game feel like playing a new game. Though I like the Witcher series, I have an axe to grind with it, that is I didn't want to play as Geralt, but I wanted to play as my character. Give me a game that plays like The Witcher, gives me choices like Baldur's Gate, and set it in the WOD. <br /> <br /> What if, instead of city building, you have territory based on clan/sect/status where you cultivated the human population. Controlling ghouls, quelling rebellions, maintaining the masquerade, and fighting off vampire incursions. That would be a cool mini game that could keep players interested after completing all of the main quests and finding all of the secrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28340-boldkill","name":"Boldkill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28340_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-25T19:05:34-08:00","id":1547249,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms, that is a good question. Ultimately, every RPG gamer wants it all, but I am reminded of why I fell in love with the WOD setting when thinking about your question. Politics! Navigating Kindred society, finding out Clan or sect secrets, surviving powerplays by manipulating elders, and carving out a niche for oneself. That has to be the difference otherwise it would become like any other vampire game, kill monsters and eat people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28340-boldkill","name":"Boldkill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28340_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-27T19:10:42-08:00","id":1547290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boldkill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546969-why-no-dark-ages-game?p=1547248#post1547248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoth, I agree with you. We need a game where choices matter, but we also need a game where there are so many different paths that it makes replaying the game feel like playing a new game. Though I like the Witcher series, I have an axe to grind with it, that is I didn't want to play as Geralt, but I wanted to play as my character. Give me a game that plays like The Witcher, gives me choices like Baldur's Gate, and set it in the WOD.<br /> <br /> What if, instead of city building, you have territory based on clan/sect/status where you cultivated the human population. Controlling ghouls, quelling rebellions, maintaining the masquerade, and fighting off vampire incursions. That would be a cool mini game that could keep players interested after completing all of the main quests and finding all of the secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you have in mind, Boldkill, is that something akin to Fallout 4 for Vampire? Because that game has exploration (with added survival needs if you play in that special mode) along with quests and the option to essentially make an attempt to create something like a civilization from the dust and ashes of the wasteland..<br /> <br /> Is something like that what you imagine? Because I'm pretty sure it could be realistically done if a larger studio put its mind to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-30T12:40:22-08:00","id":1547339,"title":"","content":"Yes 100 percent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28340-boldkill","name":"Boldkill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28340_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}